Z||000000||86GT-FstBk||09-03-2000||06:18 PM||||I'm wondering if anybody has fabricated a dash from scratch or modified the stock dash.  I would like to know how and what kind of materials were used.  Thanks<P>Brian||||reg||6
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-03-2000||07:41 PM||||I'm just starting one.  Custom dash and center console.  Door panels someday.  1/2" AC fir plywood, wood glue, small screws.  The sides and top will be covered with a good quality vinyl (fake leather) and the faces will be covered with smoked Lexan.  Center console (up to the windshield) will be 2 pieces.  One from the windshield to the shifter and the other from the shifter back to the rear window.  Digital gauges and different switches (if I can find any that work).  What did you have in mind?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||09-03-2000||10:33 PM||||Archie has a new Dash he made. Email him for some info or post a topic for him.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">   <B>1985 Sport Coupe </B><P><BR><B>Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A></B>||||reg||14
Z||000003||rockcrawl||09-04-2000||09:35 AM||||I've made a custom dash for a countach replica, not quite the same, but the same rules apply. I used 1/2" plywood for the main section, and 1/4" luan plywood for the guage housing. It was covered in 1/8" closed cell foam padding and leather look vinyl. Guages are LCD digital behind smoked lexan. You can use fiberglass and bondo on top of a wood frame to get any shape you want. My door panels and console were fiberglass with the same covering. To see pictures visit my site and click on "My Lamborghini Replica". <A HREF="http://clik.to/rockcrawl" TARGET=_blank>http://clik.to/rockcrawl</A> <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||09-05-2000||10:43 PM||||Rockcrawl, if I didn't have class first thing in the morning, I'd love to read through your site tonight... cars *and* Tesla coils.. 2 of my favorite subjects.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'll email you sometime soon (whenever I get email access.... *sigh*) with some questions regarding your custom dash..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||80's BOY||09-06-2000||12:43 PM||||i modified my dashboard alot before i put it back in. since i tossed the a/c on the rebuild and cut out the targa top, i figured i wouldn't need the a/c vents anymore. i cut the vents at an angle and mounted 4x6" speakers in them. i then cut out the center console with all the a/c and radio controls and am now building the console from front to back with a custom shifter cover and radio/crossover console. oh by the way, the factory front speaker covers were filled with bondo but i kept the defrost vent. then i had it all covered with white leather and molded to perfection. i really need a glove box if anyone has one for sale. the only bad thing is the glare from the windshield caused by the white leather. i hope to have some pics soon to put on here.||||reg||1
Z||000006||jhogans||09-06-2000||07:48 PM||||80's Boy,<P>Do you have any photos of your dash?||||reg||1
Z||000007||80's BOY||09-07-2000||09:39 AM||||yes, i have some in the bondo/chop shop stage but not any after pics yet. it turned out really nice and smooth.||||reg||3
Z||000008||whamel||09-07-2000||09:41 AM||||Probably the coolest web page on how someone designed a custom dash that I have seen is:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.perigee.net/%7elunapark/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.perigee.net/%7elunapark/</A> <BR>I'm not knocking anybody else's page, but so far this one has the best breakdown of how it went together.  It has some very informative pictures. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||09-07-2000||06:41 PM||||I've seen that before, but I'm glad you reminded me (well, not <B>just</B> me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) of it.  There are some things there that I'll need to do to my dash that I had forgotten about (foam, etc).  I don't think that dash would be very good for a daily driver.  It was meant as a sound stage for IASCA competitions (and did quite well if I remember correctly).  ||||reg||1
